<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends weaker on dollar demand.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends weaker on dollar demand.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The taka closed easier at 42.5480/5500 to the dollar in interbank trading compared with the previous 42.5430/5490, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the taka slipped further on higher demand for dollars after opening at 42.5450/5500.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates ended at 4.0-4.75 percent, down from 4.5-5.0 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
